      <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-08-07T104930_382_1786105407836_186872.webp\" alt=\"Booming Digital Marketing Career in AI Era\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/cybersecurity-professional-career-roadmap-2026-2?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-08-05T122121_005_1786351858212_930412.webp\" alt=\"Cybersecurity Professional Career Roadmap 2026\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">7. Testimonial Backlinks<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>These links are earned through customer reviews or testimonials about products or services.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Businesses encourage clients to share their experiences and feedback on different platforms and link to their websites or social media profiles. This adds credibility to their brand and boosts sales.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">8. Links from Images<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>As the name suggests, these links are added within images and redirect users to a website or website. Images can be in the form of graphs, infographics, maps, product pictures, or visual examples.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Webpages with images are likely to earn 555% more quality backlinks. Find out pages that are using your images without giving credit. Reach out to the webmaster to claim your link. You can make images more discoverable through image optimization, which includes using quality and original images with descriptive file names and alt tags.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">9. Links from Directories<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>You can acquire directory backlinks by submitting your website to local directories or business listings. Businesses with brick-and-mortar stores generally use these backlinks types in SEO to improve their <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/local-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">local SEO<\/a> effort and drive people to their physical stores.\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Google often refrains websites and businesses from mass submission to local directories. However, that doesn\u2019t mean you shouldn\u2019t build these links. Focus on linking from high-quality and reputable directories relevant to your business to make links count.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Ensure that your business information, including business name, contact details, and address, is consistent across all listings because Google is quite strict about this.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">10. Influencer-generated Backlinks<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Influencers are famous personalities with a huge following on their social media profiles. People trust them and their recommendations. They can influence buying decisions and help your brand gain popularity.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Businesses collaborate with influencers relevant to their industry to get links to their website or social media page. Google considers these links a vote of confidence from a reputed and credible source.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Moreover, influencer-generated links align with E-E-A-T algorithm. You can connect with influencers in your niche and request them to review or recommend your brand. They can post a video or image or run a contest on their page and link the post to your site.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">11. Footer Links<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>The footer is the section at the bottom of a website. Businesses use this space to place their links, which appear on every web page.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Companies use the footer section to add partner or client backlinks. These are internal links that are crucial to websites, enabling visitors to navigate and find required information without hassle. They can also be external links, such as adding a link of the company&#8217;s site that designed your office or website.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Google meticulously evaluates footer links, ensuring that websites prioritize users by providing useful or valuable links. So, don\u2019t create these links only for SEO purposes.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read: <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/seo-meta-tags\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">What Are Meta Tags in SEO? All Meta Tags Explained<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">12. Paid Links<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Paid links are those for which you pay a third-party website for a do-follow link. According to a <a href=\"https:\/\/www.authorityhacker.com\/link-building-survey\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener nofollow\">survey<\/a>, around 74% of websites pay to build links, spending an average of $83 for every link. No matter what the numbers say, paid links are considered a black-hat SEO strategy, so Google views them as a violation of search engine policies and can even penalize the site.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>They are an old and commonly used types of backlinks in digital marketing that might be against Google algorithm. Despite agreeing that paid links are not good, many businesses and marketers pay for guest posts and editorial links. However, a few quality links from top websites are worth paying. For example, paying for a guest article on a reputable site is acceptable, but you can\u2019t get a link from a private blog.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Many SEO professionals and marketers ruin their backlink profiles by acquiring numerous paid links from irrelevant sites. So, it\u2019s always better to check the page and domain authority of a site before you build a link.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-3e754c84df40274461c4ac481693818c\"><strong>Explore Key SEO Topics That You Should Know<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/seo-syllabus\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SEO Syllabus<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/seo-kpis\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SEO KPIs<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/best-free-seo-tools\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Best SEO Tools<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/search-engine-functions\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Search Engine Functions<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/local-seo-ranking-factors\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Local SEO Ranking Factors<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/best-website-speed-test-tools\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Website Speed Test Tools<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/technical-seo-checklist\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Technical SEO Checklist<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/off-page-seo-techniques\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Off Page SEO Techniques<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-factors\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">On Page SEO Factors<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/seo-chrome-extensions\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Best SEO Chrome Extensions<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-checklist\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">On Page SEO Checklist<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/seo-meta-tags\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SEO Meta Tags<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">13. Badge Backlinks<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Badges feature brands and are a sign of appreciation or recognition for industry experts. Getting a badge is a proud moment for any business. Badge backlinks are a unique link-building tactic you earn when another site awards you for your work through a digital emblem or badge, linking it back to your site.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>These badges can show certifications, achievements, contributions, or partnerships. Whenever you distribute your badge to a website, it will place it on their page. Since badges are a noticeable element on a site, they drive traffic and clicks, bringing more people to your site. Also, it will help you win the trust of visitors.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">14. PBN Backlinks<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Private Blog Network backlinks come from an unauthentic network of interlinked blogs or websites owned by a single pillar page.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>These links are not used much today as they are completely against Google\u2019s guidelines. However, some sites still use it with the primary goal of increasing their website\u2019s authority.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>PBN backlinks are known to manipulate PageRank. Therefore, it is recommended that these links be avoided. If Google discovers such a link, it can penalize your site or never consider it for search engine results.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read: <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-checklist\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Full On-Page SEO Checklist (With Strategy)\u00a0<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">15. Free Tool Backlinks<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>When you offer a free tool to anyone in your industry, you can ask them to promote it on their site and add your link. It\u2019s like a recommendation or compliment for your tool. These types of backlinks in <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/off-page-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">off-page SEO<\/a> can have a great impact on your SEO efforts, spreading the word about your tool and enticing people to try it.\u00a0<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>This free tool must be the basic version of the premium one to bring more prospects. Include a CTA to enable visitors to try it and buy the paid version.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-d72f351059e80039135382f58233f821\"><strong>Explore Our Most Popular Marketing Courses<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/digital-marketing-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogTable&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Digital Marketing Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/performance-marketing-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogTable&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Performance Marketing Course<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ws